## Run the published weights

This explicit torchvision recipe preserves the exact training/evaluation geometry and uses native safetensors weights.

```python
import torch
from PIL import Image
from torchvision.transforms import v2
from transformers import AutoModelForImageClassification

REPO = "{{ repo_id }}"
REVISION = "{{ artifact_revision }}"
model = AutoModelForImageClassification.from_pretrained(
    REPO, revision=REVISION, use_safetensors=True, trust_remote_code=False
).eval()
transform = v2.Compose([
    v2.ToImage(), v2.Resize(255, antialias=True), v2.CenterCrop(224),
    v2.ToDtype(torch.float32, scale=True),
    v2.Normalize([0.485, 0.456, 0.406], [0.229, 0.224, 0.225]),
])
image = Image.open("chest-xray.jpeg").convert("RGB")
with torch.inference_mode():
    scores = model(pixel_values=transform(image).unsqueeze(0)).logits.softmax(-1)[0]
print([(model.config.id2label[i], float(scores[i])) for i in scores.argsort(descending=True).tolist()])
```

Class order is 0 bacterial, 1 normal, 2 viral. Scores are uncalibrated model outputs. The corrected native processor includes a small MIT-licensed adapter that preserves torchvision's rounded center-crop anchor. Loading that adapter with `AutoImageProcessor` requires reviewing the pinned module and explicitly setting `trust_remote_code=True`; the standalone recipe above uses standard torchvision code.

## Data and replay

The original [Kaggle dataset](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/paultimothymooney/chest-xray-pneumonia) contains 5856 pediatric radiographs. The repository derives bacterial/viral subtypes from the original pneumonia filenames. Replaying all 624 original test images reproduces the complete stored main confusion matrix and its metrics. A saved probability/target archive allows independent recalculation.

[Source receipt](https://github.com/kiselyovd/chest-xray-classifier/blob/main/reports/provenance/chest-source.json) · [Test-file manifest](https://github.com/kiselyovd/chest-xray-classifier/blob/main/reports/provenance/chest-test-manifest.json) · [Complete processor comparison](https://github.com/kiselyovd/chest-xray-classifier/blob/main/reports/provenance/processor-full-test-parity.json).

Historical training membership and patient-level independence are unrecorded. This is research on a limited pediatric cohort; clinical validation has not been performed.

